    "details": "<p><strong>Code Kernel '26</strong> | Decode &rarr; Build &rarr; Prove</p>\n<p>An online national problem-solving competition by <strong>X-Kernel</strong>, the student-led technical and innovation club of <strong>Gokaraju Rangaraju Institute of Engineering and Technology (GRIET), Hyderabad</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Tentative dates:</strong> 12 October &ndash; 21 October 2026<br /><strong>Mode:</strong> Online<br /><strong>Team size:</strong> 1 to 4 engineering students<br /><strong>Format:</strong> Decode &rarr; Build &rarr; Prove</p>\n<p><strong>What It Is</strong><br />Engineering Students Enter in Teams of 1 to 4. Each Team Takes One Real Problem Through Three Stages in Order. This Is <em>Not</em> a Pitch Contest and <em>Not</em> a Prototype-Only Hackathon. The work has to hold up when the Test Changes.</p>\n<p><strong>Stages</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Decode</strong> &mdash; Understand the Real Problem Before Writing a Solution. Root Cause, People Affected, Limits Already in Place, and Whether the Approach Can Work.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Build</strong> &mdash; Make a Practical Response, Not a Slide. Software, Ai/ml, Web or Mobile, Automation, Data, a Technical or Business Solution, a Hardware Simulation, or A Proof of Concept.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Prove</strong> &mdash; Show that It Still Works when The Test Changes. Unseen Checks, Extra Constraints, New Test Cases, a Technical Evaluation, a Live Demo and Questions.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Problems</strong><br />Each Problem Is Framed as <strong>Problem, Context, Constraints and Expected Outcome</strong>. Sponsor Partners May Contribute Problem Statements. the Day-By-Day Round Calendar Inside the Tentative Window Is to Be Decided.</p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to <strong>Engineering Students Across India</strong></li>\n<li>Teams of <strong>1 to 4</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Online</strong> participation</li>\n</ul>",
    "end_date": "2026-10-20T00:00:00+05:30",
